data/acceptance_criteria","value":"Require completeness.status=complete with safe-integer zero unreadable counts; require omission_receipt has_omissions=false, safe-integer zero count, and empty groups; require read_output contract v1 for list with within_budget=true, no compaction or omission, and complete include/amount/cost dimensions; reject output budget truncation/exceeded disclosures; return stable independent finding codes with absent, malformed, contradictory, and nonzero negative controls; emit canonical executable current recovery and prove it in a fresh-tracker acceptance test"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-usfg"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"GitHub issue #1078"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.21 public SDK"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Obtain the real pm list --all strict unbounded JSON envelope, then independently delete omission_receipt, contradict its count/groups, delete read_output, or set completeness unreadable_item_count=1; certifyCompleteListResult currently accepts each mutated envelope. Inspect PmCompleteListValidationError.recovery.suggested_retry for stale list-all syntax."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Certification fails closed unless completeness, omission_receipt, and read_output independently prove complete unbounded delivery with stable finding codes; budget truncation disclosures are rejected; the canonical suggested retry uses list --all, output-include full, output-budget unbounded, and output-limit unbounded and executes successfully in a fresh tracker."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Missing or contradictory truth receipts are accepted and certified; recovery suggests pm list-all --full --strict-read --no-truncate --output-budget unbounded --json."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.8.21"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"SDK complete-list certification"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/regression","value":true},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-y4aaol","kind":"incident_from","created_at":"2026-08-21T12:55:33.362Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-21T12:55:33.362Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"text=Duplicate check 2026-08-21: searched all-status PM corpus for GH-1078, certifyCompleteListResult, contradictory receipts, complete-list certification, and stale list-all recovery. No duplicate exists. pm-y4aaol is the closed predecessor that shipped the first complete-list certificate and pm-usfg is the canonical open SDK-first parent; linked with incident_from plus scalar parent rather than a generic related edge. GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1078"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"0898140986fb5822a83103468050f8b095ecc5576a50a704c6bd0d7dc15e4fec","item_hash_version":2,"message":""}
